"""the palette manager's colours come from the brand, through brand_map.json, and
every colour value its tests use is named once

    python up.py             # apply, then run the guards and CI's own commands
    python up.py --check     # rehearse every edit in memory, write nothing
    python up.py --verify    # run the guards and CI's commands, change nothing

For rnv-color-palette-manager, derived against a fresh clone at the live head
(01e5f25, which is 8ad8709 with the earlier up.py). This ONE script replaces
that up.py and the alignment script sent after it: put it in place of up.py
and run it. Every file it edits is held to the head's, and it refuses if one
moved.

RNV-DELIVERY-SCRIPT-DO-NOT-SWEEP. This script is a delivery tool, not
application source, and it names what it retires. That marker is what tells
this fleet's scanners to skip it.

RULED 2026-10-16: the colour-sync proposal, #36 to #46, piloted here; #47 A,
the other four apps the same way, with one shared tool, test and workflow, and
the charcoal panel colour following APP.panel in every app.
RULED 2026-10-17: #52 A, the application's own colours read by name in the
tests too; #53 A, every other colour value a test needs named once, in
tests/colour_values.py, under a guard; #54 A, a colour value is a string that
is only a colour; #55 B, the root suite as well; #56 A, colour values in the
application's own code named in the colour file; #57 A, no hex code in a
test's sentences either: the name, and the value printed through it.
RULED 2026-10-18: #58 A, the HSL clipboard example in Settings is made the way
a copy is made, so it is what the clipboard will hold.

WHAT LANDS.
  brand_map.json               where each of 31 colours in ui/colors.py comes from:
                               14 brand names, 17 the application's own, each with
                               its reason
  tools/sync_colors.py         writes those values into ui/colors.py, and
                               COLORS.md, from the map and the pinned brand;
                               the same file in all five applications
  ui/colors.py                 a note at the top and a marker on 31 lines;
                               CLIPBOARD_PREVIEW_COLOR named (#56 A).
                               NO VALUE MOVES
  COLORS.md                    the application's colour chart
  tests/test_colours_in_sync.py  every value, once, against the brand
  .github/workflows/brand-sync.yml  the daily check
  tests/colour_values.py       every other colour value the tests use, named
                               once, with why (#53 A)
  tests/test_colour_values.py  the guard: no colour value, and no hex code in a
                               sentence, anywhere else in the tests
  24 test files                an application colour read by name; every other
                               value read from tests/colour_values.py
  test_rnv_palette_manager.py  the same, in the root suite (#55 B)
  ui/settings_dialog.py        the clipboard examples made from
                               CLIPBOARD_PREVIEW_COLOR (#56 A); the HSL one the
                               way a copy makes it (#58 A)
  tests/test_qt_color_slot.py  each example is what a copy writes (#58 A)
  README.md                    the new files in the project tree

THE DAILY CHECK NEEDS ONE SETTING: Settings > Actions > General > Workflow
permissions > "Allow GitHub Actions to create and approve pull requests".
"""
